  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Subburaj M vs State Of Kerala on 6 August, 2025 Author: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Bench: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Op (Crl.) No.445 of 2025 2025:Ker:58906 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.V.Kunhikrishnan Wednesday, The 6Th Day Of August 2025 / 15Th Sravana, 1947 Op(Crl.) No. 445 Of 2025 Crime No.703/2019 Of Chevayur Police Station, Kozhikode Against The Order/Judgment Dated In Rc No.149 Of 2022 Of Judicial Magistrate Of First Class -I,Kozhikode Petitioner(S)/Accused Persons: 1 Subburaj M Aged 53 Years, S/O. Mookkaiah Appu Nivas Chitrapuram Idukki District, Pin - 685565 2 Anil Kumar T Aged 53 Years, S/O. Subramanyan T, Thayyil House, Vallikkunnu North, Near Kotta Temple Malappuram District, Pin - 673314 3 Abdu Raheem Valiya Parakkal Aged 44 Years, S/O. Moosa V.P., Valiya Parakkal House, Kuzhippuram Chenakkal. Mattathur Post, Malappuram District, Pin - 676528 By Advs. Sri.Shashank Devan Sri.K.M.Aneesh Sri.Adarsh Kumar Shri.Yadu Krishnan P.M. Subburaj M vs State Of Kerala on 6 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18824555/ 1 Respondent(S)/State And Defacto Complainant: 1 State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam, Pin - 682031 Op (Crl.) No.445 of 2025 2025:Ker:58906 2 2 Food Safety Commissioner Office Of Commissioner Of Food Safety, Thycaud P.O., Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala, Pin - 695014 By Adv: Sr Pp, Sri Hrithwik C S This Op (Criminal) Having Come Up For Admission On 06.08.2025, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: Op (Crl.) No.445 of 2025 2025:Ker:58906 3 P.V.Kunhikrishnan, J. ------------------------------------------- Op (Crl) No.445 of 2025 -------------------------------------------- Dated this the 06th day of August, 2025 Judgment",
    "facts": "The 1st petitioner is the accused in Crime No.703/2019 of Chevayur Police Station, Kozhikode. The above case was referred by the police after 2025:KER:58906 investigation in the year 2022. The case was numbered by the Judicial First Class Magistrate Court-I, Kozhikode as RC 149/2022. The grievance of the petitioner is that, based on Ext.P7 proceedings of the Food Safety Commissioner, the learned Magistrate is not proceeding with RC No.149/2022. I am of the considered opinion that the Food Safety Commissioner has no authority to dictate to a Magistrate Court not to close the referred case till a decision is taken by the Government. The Registry will get a report from the Judicial First Class Magistrate-I, Kozhikode to find out why no further steps are taken in RC No.149/2022 and if it is based on Ext.P7, which is not binding to the Magistrate. \"In obedience to reference cited above, I may respectfully submit that the Station House Officer filed a refer report in Crime No. 703/19 of Chevayoor police Station on Subburaj M vs State Of Kerala on 6 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18824555/ 3 24.02.2022 and a notice was issued to the Food Safety Commissioner, the complainant of this case. The same day, the Food Safety Commissioner, the complainant of this case, filed a letter NO.CFS/781/2022-G dated 12.12.2024 stating that the proceedings in this case should not be disposed of until a final decision from the government is obtained. On 03.03.2025, the complainant was absent and there was no 2025:KER:58906 representation, case was posted to 03.05.2025, 24.06.2025 and 03.09.2025 respectively. It is humbly submitted that, I joined this office on 18.5.2025. The case was already posted for report on the basis of the letter received from food safety commissioner. From 3.3.25 onwards, the case was adjourned to 3.5.25 and to 24.6.25 before I joined this office on 24.6.25, I, in continuation to the earlier proceedings, posted the case for report on a wrong notion, inadvertently.",
